course: dictionary
lesson: 8371
title: Route: the way from here to there
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A route is the way you go to get from one place to another. «Telling someone your route and return time means help can start looking for you quickly.» If people know your route, they know where to look for you.
explain: A bus route is the set way a bus takes, with its stops along the way. To route something is to send it a certain way, like a parcel or a message. Read the words around route to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Some route words come in phrases. «The quickest route» is the way that takes the least time. An «escape route» or a «fire escape route» is a way out of danger. Read the whole phrase, because one word on its own can hide the meaning.
fact: A route is a way from one place to another.
fact: A bus route is the set way a bus takes, with its stops.
fact: «Trade routes» were paths that carried goods from one place to another.
fact: A route-finding algorithm adds up the time for each possible road and picks the shortest total.
fact: An algorithm is just a clear list of steps, like a recipe.
exercise: Mum says, «Plan a safe route to school, with crossings and lights.» What is a route? | A lesson on maps | A kind of school bag | *The way you go from home to school | A school trip with a teacher
exercise: «The bus route has six stops before the park.» What is a bus route? | A bus that has broken down | *The set way a bus takes, with its stops | The seat where the driver sits | A road closed for building work
exercise: Ella says, «The sat nav found the quickest route to the beach.» What does the quickest route mean? | The road with the most cars | The longest way round | *The way that takes the least time | The way with the most turns
test: «Real ships sailed with the monsoon, and the way out and the way back were different routes.» What does routes mean here? | Ships that are very big | Winds that blow only in summer | *The ways you go from one place to another | Sailors' songs
test: To route a parcel means what? | *To send it a certain way | To wrap it in paper | To open it carefully | To weigh it at the post office
exam: «Telling someone your route and return time means help can start looking for you quickly.» Why does telling someone your route help? | *Helpers know where to look for you quickly | Your route becomes shorter | Your phone battery lasts longer | The bus driver can stop the bus
